ue" class=3D"wp-block-spacer"></div><h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading">What are=
 artichoke tacos?</h2><p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">We love cooking Mexic=
an food at home. It=E2=80=99s not been long since I posted my <a href=3D"ht=
tps://forkfulofplants.com/vegan-jackfruit-enchiladas/">jackfruit enchiladas=
</a>, and my <a href=3D"https://forkfulofplants.com/mexican-buddha-bowl-faj=
ita-veg/">Mexican inspired Buddha bowl</a> is a firm favourite here on the =
blog.&nbsp;</p><p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">I know what you might be thi=
nking- artichokes are a strange choice for a taco filling! This one is a li=
ttle bit different, but I love what artichokes bring to the party. They mak=
e a tasty, whole-food alternative to vegan fish tacos.</p><p class=3D"wp-bl=
ock-paragraph">Artichokes have a soft and mild flavour which means they don=
=E2=80=99t overwhelm the flavour of the marinade. They also have a meaty, t=
ender and slightly flaky texture. When marinated, breaded and baked they go=
 crispy on the outside and chewy and flaky on the inside.</p><p class=3D"wp=
-block-paragraph">To keep the artichoke tacos healthy, I=E2=80=99ve baked t=
he artichokes for this recipe rather than frying. This also makes it super =
easy to follow, with only a small amount of hands-on time needed.</p><div s=
tyle=3D"height:30px" aria-hidden=3D"true" class=3D"wp-block-spacer"></div><=
h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading">So what exactly is in vegan fish tacos?</h2><=
p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">The star of the show with these tacos is the=
 artichokes. Canned artichokes are marinated until they take on a mild fish=
y flavour. They=E2=80=99re then lightly battered and breaded, and baked in =
the oven until they=E2=80=99re crispy and golden.</p><p class=3D"wp-block-p=
aragraph">The artichokes are served very simply, in a soft taco shell with =
sliced avocado, chopped tomatoes (or <a href=3D"https://forkfulofplants.com=
/pico-de-gallo-coriander-free/">pico de gallo</a>), quick pickled red cabba=
ge, green onion and a quick dill mayo.</p><div style=3D"height:30px" aria-h=
idden=3D"true" class=3D"wp-block-spacer"></div><h3 class=3D"wp-block-headin=
g">What makes the artichokes taste like fish?&nbsp;</h3><p class=3D"wp-bloc=
k-paragraph">As the vegan =E2=80=98fish=E2=80=99 is in a taco, we don=E2=80=
=99t want it to be too overwhelmingly fishy in flavour. To get that light =
=E2=80=98fishy=E2=80=99 taste, a marinade is made from almond milk, chickpe=
a flour, caper brine and lemon zest and juice. Once the artichokes have bee=
n marinated, they=E2=80=99re battered and breaded in a mixture of panko bre=
adcrumbs, old bay seasoning, mixed herbs and seaweed flakes.&nbsp;</p><div =
style=3D"height:30px" aria-hidden=3D"true" class=3D"wp-block-spacer"></div>=
