lass=3D"wp-block-heading">What key ingredients are needed for this recipe?<=
/h2><p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Artichokes</strong>=E2=80=93 Fo=
r artichoke tacos, you need to use the kind of artichokes which have been c=
ooked and frozen or <a href=3D"https://amzn.to/3AyNzQV" target=3D"_blank" r=
el=3D"noreferrer noopener nofollow">canned</a>. Those that have been marina=
ted or stored in olive oil won=E2=80=99t be suitable for vegan fish tacos, =
as they will already have a noticeable flavour to them. Fresh artichokes ar=
e delicious but a lot of work, and I wanted to keep this one simple. With c=
anned or frozen artichokes, all the work is done.</p><p class=3D"wp-block-p=
aragraph"><strong>Taco shells</strong>=E2=80=93 I=E2=80=99ve used soft whea=
t tacos, as I find them easier to work with. If you want to keep it a bit h=
ealthier, use wholewheat tacos. Alternatively, corn tacos would be more tra=
ditional and would be gluten free.</p><p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph"><stro=
ng>Breadcrumbs</strong>=E2=80=93 <a href=3D"https://amzn.to/2X6TwXE" target=
=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer noopener nofollow">Panko breadcrumbs</a> crea=
te the best crispy texture for the coating. You can buy these from the stor=
e to keep it easy.&nbsp;</p><p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Seaweed=
</strong>=E2=80=93 I use a product called Shony which is a mixture of red, =
green and brown flaked seaweed.&nbsp; If you can=E2=80=99t get hold of this=
 product, any kind of seaweed flakes would work- such as nori or <a href=3D=
"https://amzn.to/2X9qdnn" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer noopener nofo=
llow">dulse flakes</a>.&nbsp;</p><p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Qu=
ick pickled cabbage</strong>=E2=80=93 Once the artichokes have gone into th=
e oven, mix the sliced red cabbage with vinegar, and a pinch of sugar and s=
alt. By the time the artichoke tacos are ready, your cabbage will be bright=
 pink and lightly pickled.</p><p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph"><strong>For t=
he mayo</strong>=E2=80=93 For the mayo, simply combine your favourite vegan=
 mayonnaise with chopped dill, lemon juice, and chopped capers. It=E2=80=99=
s the perfect accompaniment to vegan fish tacos and accentuates the fishy f=
lavour.</p><div style=3D"height:30px" aria-hidden=3D"true" class=3D"wp-bloc=
